1. To create the new branch we hv 2 ways:
    a. Create in UI itself.

    b. Create from CLI
        To create a branch only : git checkout <branch name>
        To create and checkout to that branch : git checkout -b <branch name>

2. To work in multiple branches:
    a. clone the main branch to local.
    b. In VS code in the bottom we hv branch icon, using that we can navigate / work on any branch.
    c. To check the current branch where we in:
        git branch   : It shows the * infront of branch, that is the active branch.

3. To push the data from branch:
    a. first time use the below command.
        git push -u origin <branch name>

    b. next time 
        git push --all
        